            <ArticleTitle>Percutaneous transluminal coronary angioplasty of anomalous right coronary artery.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>39-41</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Coronary angioplasty of tortuous anomalous coronary arteries can be technically challenging. We describe a successful percutaneous transluminal coronary angioplasty (PTCA) of an anomalous right coronary artery after a failed previous attempt. The anatomic limitations of anomalous right coronary arteries and technical considerations for PTCA are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
